window.docContents[25].resolve({"/Storage-and-commands/Loops/#Core-C______--Storage-and-commands--Loops":{"contents":"The rule While-T recurs on its own conclusion. A return in the body interrupts the loop, rule While-Ret. The divergence of while (true) {} has no derivation, a limitation of inductive big step semantics (Kahn, RR-0601, §4.3, p. 11).\n\nThe rule For defines for through while. The variable of the initialiser has the loop as its scope, and the loop frees its location at exit,  of . The body is a block of its own, and the step runs after the body, outside the body's scope. The type checker checks the step under  and discards its context . The initialiser ends with .\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Storage and commands","header":"4.6. Loops","id":"/Storage-and-commands/Loops/#Core-C______--Storage-and-commands--Loops"}});